  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ETHNO-PROGRAM FOR THE SUSTAINABLE CONSERVATION OF THE DAHL&apos;S TOAD-HEADED TURTLE (MESOCLEMMYS DAHLI) IN COLOMBIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT CONSERVATION ACTIVITIES IN COLLABORATION WITH LOCAL ZENU COMMUNITIES TO PROTECT THE CARRANCHINA TURTLE. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE 1 STRENGTHENING THE CAPACITY OF 1,000 RIVERINE INDIGENOUS ZENU PEOPLE IN FRESHWATER TURTLE CONSERVATION PRACTICES 2 CREATING 32 KM2 OF PROTECTED RIVER AND RIVERINE HABITAT FOR NESTING, FORAGING AND MATING OF THIS SPECIES 3 ESTABLISHING A REGIONAL OFFICE LED BY THE ZENU WITH THE GOAL TO PROTECT FRESHWATER TURTLES ON THE SINU RIVER AND 4 MONITORING OF 17 KM2 OF RIVERSIDE NESTING ZONES TO PROTECT AGAINST ILLEGAL TRAFFICKING OF THE CARRANCHINA TURTLE AND OTHER TURTLE SPECIES.</narrative>
  </description>
